  "natural_language_conclusion": "The content-separating representation created a materially larger A-versus-B action-kernel response than raw bytes, so the real actor path can distinguish the registered payload bodies. The fixed reward-only training run did not turn that capacity into a stable positive CORRECT-versus-SWAPPED or CORRECT-versus-NATIVE_NEUTRAL return contrast: seeds 86031 and 86032 were mixed and close to zero, while seed 86033 was consistently negative and drove the negative overall content-encoder mean. This is a valid nonconfirmatory B diagnostic, not a scientific disposition or a direction decision.",
  "interpretation_limits": [
    "The content encoder intervention changes all four registered slot embeddings, including empty and native-neutral, not only A/B separability.",
    "No untrained three-arm outcome baseline was run; initial and trained A/B kernel diagnostics bound representation sensitivity but do not by themselves identify reward causation.",
